neage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"956f7ff596c94168b92a6763b101c2c609933ce3beb96a462bd4f54e8855a8fc"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":5689,"output_tokens":451,"requests":1}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"30b6c05c1bf85bf849beed22a97f5f5471cf5d158cb3685067bfd3f52ca5e141"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":4466,"output_tokens":699,"requests":1}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"bfb3586004846a35008d09c86c41d215d7029bd84feb815e4be8bc6e74f63952"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":116861,"output_tokens":1454,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"882e13e776660546c386fd951916b2269764cbf8deb1316ecf70beb695d76974"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":198583,"output_tokens":4285,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"80bb259858664c4937b9776b5ad5ed6d9889a49e049ed6c6b33b2f3eff186bc8"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":123018,"output_tokens":1554,"requests":3}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] For coupled-value secrets (rebar-bot-signing-key ↔ GHA REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY; ci-gerrit-ssh-key ↔ GHA GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY), require the SSM value and the mirrored external copy be set to the SAME value in the same rotation step, and add verification that both copies match.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ssm.tf:57-61 'The same private key is also stored as the GitHub Actions secret REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY for the reconcile-bridge + canary workflows.'","ssm.tf:44-46 'ci-gerrit-ssh-key: ... an operator copies its value into the GitHub Actions secret GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY so the workflow can SSH back into Gerrit :29418 to cast Verified.'","Parent ticket auspicial-wily-warbler / gnarly-sinistrous-groundhog comment: 'rebar-bot-signing-key ... also mirrored to GHA secret REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY — must rotate the pair together.'"],"finding":"The plan treats each secret as an independently-rotatable unit but two listed secrets are COUPLED-VALUE: rebar-bot-signing-key must equal GHA secret REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY, and ci-gerrit-ssh-key must equal GHA secret GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY. If the SSM value and the mirrored GHA copy are not set to the identical value in the same operation, the CI Verified-vote / reconcile-bridge paths break. The plan's per-secret AC framing has no atomic 'update both copies to the same value' requirement.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1d2687c82ae2ef31","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'Each listed secret is rotated by an operator who can reissue/update the corresponding external credential or trust store.'","norm_id":"n37794e2d57ff03c2","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator rotates the SSM value for rebar-bot-signing-key but forgets to update the GHA secret, so signature verification in the reconcile-bridge workflow starts failing.","SSM ci-gerrit-ssh-key and GHA GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY drift, breaking the CI Verified-vote SSH path into Gerrit."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC clause: 'For secrets mirrored into an external store as an identical value (rebar-bot-signing-key/REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY, ci-gerrit-ssh-key/GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY), update both copies to the same new value in one operation and verify the dependent workflow (reconcile-bridge / CI Verified-vote) succeeds post-rotation.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the consumer-health AC to name non-restart trust updates: COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET requires a coordinated LMN edge-gate (lmn-sso-gate/lmn-staging-sso-gate) redeploy, and gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key requires updating dependent clients' known_hosts (incl. CI), each verified before the rotation is called complete.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["auth_sso.tf:33-39 cookie key 'auth-host Lambda reads it at RUNTIME ... Rotating invalidates ALL live sessions.'","Parent ticket comment: cookie key 'baked into Lambda@Edge bundles at deploy ... Rotating the SSM value -> ... modernization-navigator production SSO breaks until LMN redeploys its edge bundles.'","Parent ticket comment: gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key 'SSH host key — rotating trips known_hosts for every client incl. CI's SSH-to-Gerrit Verified-vote path.'"],"finding":"The 'Every affected consumer is restarted/redeployed and verified healthy' AC does not capture two non-restart break modes documented in the codebase/parent investigation: COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET is baked into another team's (LMN) Lambda@Edge bundles at deploy — rotating the SSM value breaks modernization-navigator production SSO until LMN redeploys its edge gates (a cross-team redeploy, not a local consumer restart); and gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key rotation trips known_hosts for every SSH client (incl. CI's SSH-to-Gerrit path), which is a client-trust update, not a consumer restart.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3be5e2c94d076cfa","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'Every affected consumer is restarted/redeployed and verified healthy after its rotation.' / Verification section","norm_id":"nb0de26e653a9c251","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator rotates COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET and restarts the auth-host Lambda, marks it healthy, but LMN's edge gates still verify with the old key — modernization-navigator SSO is down.","Operator rotates the Gerrit SSH host key; CI and other SSH clients fail host-key verification until known_hosts is updated — not captured by 'restart consumer'."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the per-secret rotation ordering/coordination contract (external trust-store update vs SSM version advance vs consumer restart), including any dual-credential grace/overlap window, so the read-old-credential window is bounded.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.548,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Every affected consumer is restarted/redeployed and verified healthy after its rotation.' — states post-rotation health but not the rotation/trust-update/restart ordering","ABSENCE: no statement of whether the external trust store is updated before or after the SSM version advances, nor how the read-old-credential window is bounded (dual-key/grace-period overlap vs hard cutover)"],"finding":"The rotation plan updates shared state (AWS SSM parameters that consumers read) but does not specify the ordering/coordination contract for the window between advancing the SSM parameter and updating the external trust store and restarting consumers. For externally anchored keys (e.g. gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key, github-replication-deploy-key, github-oauth-client-secret), a consumer or external party may hold the old credential (now invalid) or the external trust store may not yet accept the new one, causing an outage window if not sequenced.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"feef860e36167ab13","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria / Verification","norm_id":"nd15989509f09a21f","priority":0.402,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an acceptance criterion requiring, for each secret, an explicit cutover sequence (e.g. add-new-then-remove-old with overlap for keys that support it; or a scheduled maintenance window for hard cutovers) and a bound on the window where old/new credentials coexist.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"hard","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item 'Every affected consumer is restarted/redeployed and verified healthy after its r' cites operational evidence (deploy) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is veri